    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\ntrailspace, starter\n\n### Description\n\nSpaces are erroneously highlighted on the start screen, even with `only_in_normal_buffers` enabled. Once any window or buffer changes occur, the highlighting disappears.\r\n\r\nTrailspace creates an autocommand that watches for `buftype` changes. When starter loads, it sets `buftype`. Perhaps there's a race on `buftype` somewhere, where:\r\n\r\n1. trailspace reads buftype (`''`)\r\n2. starter sets buftype (`nofile`)\r\n3. trailspace watches for buftype changes\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.7.3\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Put spaces somewhere in starter's config. I put mine in the header (https://github.com/assistcontrol/vim/blob/main/lua/aw/plugins/ministarter.lua).\r\n2. Loading order of starter vs trailspace seems not to matter.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n_No response_\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nTrailing spaces are highlighted.\r\n\r\n`:set buftype=nofile` turns highlighting off. So does anything that switches windows (create window, `:h`, etc.).",
