        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for noticing this!\r\n\r\nThe reason for this is that Starter buffer is designed to open as fast as possible. One of the tricks that gave a massive speedup was setting buffer filetype and all buffer options with `noautocmd` (which disables autocommands from 'mini.trailspace'). To balance this, there is a `MiniStarterOpened` custom event with which users can operate upon buffer opening.\r\n\r\nSo in your case adding `vim.cmd('autocmd User MiniStarterOpened lua MiniTrailspace.unhighlight()')` to your config should solve this.\r\n\r\nHowever, I agree that this is an issue. I'll try to find a good way to solve this while preserving startup speed. So let's not close this yet.",
